          <p>
            Ignore the tank number and read the first-hour rating, which is the gallons of hot water the unit can deliver in an hour starting from full — the figure that actually predicts whether the third shower is warm. Two units with the same 50 gallon tank can differ by 20 gallons of first-hour rating depending on element size and control strategy.
